From: Holodor <holodor@bonesaw.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6afe: the DisplayPort DEVICE_START is acknowledged at the DP audio engine's edge

Traced on the Retroid Pocket 5 (SM8250, vendor ADSP firmware; ftrace +
kprobes on afe_apr_send_pkt, q6afe_callback, apr_callback,
qcom_glink_native_rx and msm_dp_audio_enable, 2026-10-15): the DSP
acknowledges AFE_PORT_CMD_DEVICE_START for DISPLAY_PORT_RX only after the
DP audio engine's rising edge. ROCKNIX's "drm/display: add hw_params
callback to hdmi audio ops" made the engine come up at hw_params, before
this start; the DSP then missed the edge in ~40 % of the starts, held the
acknowledgement until the next engine transition, and the stream (or
PipeWire's one-time card probe, which marks the profile unsupported) was
lost after a 3 s timeout. Toggling the engine afterwards or stopping and
restarting the port (EFAILED / EALREADY) does not recover it.

Without that patch upstream's hdmi-codec enables the engine in its
prepare, which runs after this DAI's prepare, so the acknowledgement
cannot arrive while q6afe waits. Wait 150 ms for that one command, report
the port started, and let the codec prepare raise the engine; the
acknowledgement follows at once. Measured: every start acknowledged at
the edge, 6/6 streams and the card probe play (docked boot, kernel 39).
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c	2026-10-15 15:13:21.192723344 +0900
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c	2026-10-15 16:02:42.294781545 +0900
@@ -1046,6 +1046,28 @@
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(q6afe_get_port_id);
 
+/*
+ * HOLODOR: the DSP acknowledges DEVICE_START for the DisplayPort port only
+ * after the DP audio engine's rising edge. With the engine switched on by the
+ * hdmi-codec's prepare (after this DAI's prepare, as upstream orders it) the
+ * acknowledgement cannot arrive while we wait here, so do not wait 3 s and
+ * fail: wait briefly, report the port started, and let the codec prepare
+ * raise the engine; the acknowledgement follows at once and the callback
+ * stores it. Retroid Pocket 5 (SM8250), ftrace + kprobes 2026-10-15: with the
+ * engine already on at START the acknowledgement was held in ~40 % of the
+ * starts (the DSP had missed the edge) and the stream was lost; with this
+ * order every start is held exactly until the edge and every stream plays.
+ */
+#define DP_START_TIMEOUT_MS 150
+
+static unsigned int afe_cmd_timeout_ms(struct q6afe_port *port, uint32_t rsp_opcode)
+{
+	if (port && port->id == AFE_PORT_ID_HDMI_OVER_DP_RX &&
+	    rsp_opcode == AFE_PORT_CMD_DEVICE_START)
+		return DP_START_TIMEOUT_MS;
+	return TIMEOUT_MS;
+}
+
 static int afe_apr_send_pkt(struct q6afe *afe, struct apr_pkt *pkt,
 			    struct q6afe_port *port, uint32_t rsp_opcode)
 {
@@ -1073,7 +1095,7 @@
 	}
 
 	ret = wait_event_timeout(*wait, (result->opcode == rsp_opcode),
-				 msecs_to_jiffies(TIMEOUT_MS));
+				 msecs_to_jiffies(afe_cmd_timeout_ms(port, rsp_opcode)));
 	if (!ret) {
 		ret = -ETIMEDOUT;
 	} else if (result->status > 0) {
@@ -1731,7 +1753,11 @@
 	start->port_id = port_id;
 
 	ret = afe_apr_send_pkt(afe, pkt, port, AFE_PORT_CMD_DEVICE_START);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT && port_id == AFE_PORT_ID_HDMI_OVER_DP_RX) {
+		/* see afe_cmd_timeout_ms(): started, acknowledged at the engine edge */
+		dev_dbg(afe->dev, "DisplayPort DEVICE_START ack held by the DSP, continuing\n");
+		ret = 0;
+	} else if (ret)
 		dev_err(afe->dev, "AFE enable for port 0x%x failed %d\n",
 			port_id, ret);
 
